<Prose title="Privacy" description="Shot collects nothing. Neither does this site.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>Shot doesn’t collect anything about you, and neither does this website.</p>

  <h2 id="app">The app</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>No account, no analytics, no crash reporting.</strong> Shot never sends your captures, usage or device details anywhere.</li>
    <li><strong>Captures stay on your Mac,</strong> in the folder you choose (<code>~/Pictures/Shot</code> by default), or in a temporary folder when saving is off.</li>
    <li><strong>The only network request is the update check.</strong> The second time you open Shot, it asks whether to check for updates. If you agree, it downloads the update feed from GitHub once a day. You can turn this off in Settings › About.</li>
    <li><strong>Permissions are asked for only when needed.</strong> Screen Recording is needed for any capture. Microphone and Camera are asked for the first time you record with them.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Shot is open source, and you can <a href="https://github.com/LorcanChinnock/shot">read the code</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="site">This website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No cookies, no analytics, no tracking pixels, no third-party fonts or scripts.</li>
    <li>It’s served by Cloudflare, which processes standard request data (such as your IP address) to deliver and protect the site. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a>.</li>
    <li>Downloads come from GitHub Releases, under <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="contact">Questions</h2>
  <p>Open an issue on <a href="https://github.com/LorcanChinnock/shot/issues">GitHub</a>.</p>
</Prose>
